<title>FINLAND: MONETARY STABILITY KEY ERM ISSUE - NIINISTO.</title>
<headline>MONETARY STABILITY KEY ERM ISSUE - NIINISTO.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto said on Thursday the key issue when deciding on fixing the markka to Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism was if joining ERM would improve monetary stability.</p>
<p>&quot;The government regards as central the question whether ERM membership will improve conditions for monetary stability in Finland,&quot; Niinisto said.</p>
<p>He was addressing a parliament question-and-answer session.  </p>
<p>Niinisto repeated that the government will decide this autumn whether to link the markka to ERM.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
